"Allah renders worthless the deeds of those who disbelieve and avert people from the path of Allah. In contrast, for those who believe, perform righteous deeds, and believe in what has been revealed to Muhammad, He pardons their sins and rectifies their state. The fundamental difference between these two groups is that the disbelievers follow falsehood, while the believers follow the truth from their Lord. Thus does Allah present their examples to people.\n\nWhen you encounter the disbelievers in battle, strike their necks. Once you have overcome their strength, bind the captives securely. Thereafter, either release them freely or take ransom. This ayah offers options to the leader regarding captives: executing them, enslaving them, releasing them for ransom, or setting them free without compensation. However, the scholars differed on this matter; while some state that this ruling was abrogated by the verses in Surah at-Tawbah, others maintain that it is definitive (muhkam). According to al-Tabari, both verses are valid, and the leader has discretion.\n\nThe deeds of those slain in the path of Allah will not be in vain. Allah guides them, rectifies their state, and admits them into Paradise. Paradise has been made known to them in this world and adorned with sweet fragrances. If the believers help Allah (by upholding His commands and serving His religion), Allah will also help them and make their feet firm.\n\nAs for the disbelievers, ruin awaits them and their deeds will come to nothing. That is because they disliked what Allah revealed. Have they not traveled through the earth and seen the end of those before them? Allah destroyed them. The same fate applies to these disbelievers as well. Allah is the protector and helper of the believers, whereas the disbelievers have no protector.\n\nAllah admits those who believe and perform righteous deeds into gardens beneath which rivers flow. The disbelievers, on the other hand, eat and drink like cattle in this world, and their destination is the Fire. How many cities far stronger than the city that drove you out have been destroyed! Is one who relies on clear evidence from his Lord like one whose evil deeds are made appealing to him and who follows his own desires?\n\nThe description of the Paradise promised to the righteous: In it are rivers of incorruptible water, rivers of milk whose taste never changes, rivers of wine delicious to those who drink it, and rivers of purified honey.\n\nAllah will admit those who believe and do righteous deeds into gardens beneath which rivers flow. Those who disbelieve indulge in worldly pleasures, eating and drinking like cattle, and their final destination is the Fire. While there are all kinds of fruits and forgiveness from their Lord in Paradise for the believers, the disbelievers are made to drink boiling water that tears their bowels to pieces. These two groups are not alike at all.\n\nThe representation of the Paradise promised to the righteous is as follows: In it are rivers of incorruptible water, milk whose taste never alters, delicious and non-intoxicating wine, and pure, filtered honey. Moreover, there are all kinds of fruits and forgiveness from their Lord. This forgiveness has been interpreted as never reminding them of their sins, or as bounty and good pleasure. While the people of Paradise abide eternally amid these blessings, the people of Hell will be tormented with boiling water.\n\nThe hypocrites come to the gathering of the Messenger of Allah and listen to his words, yet they treat them lightly. When they depart from his presence, they ask the knowledgeable Companions mockingly, \"What did he just say?\" Allah has sealed their hearts; they follow their whims and desires. As for those who are guided, Allah increases their guidance and inspires them with piety. The portents of the Hour have come; they will not believe until the punishment comes upon them suddenly.\n\nO Muhammad! Know that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah. Ask forgiveness both for your own sin and for the believing men and believing women. Allah knows your movements and your place of rest. This is a conclusion to the explanations given since the beginning of the surah. This seeking of forgiveness (istighfar) will find its response in the upcoming Surah al-Fath.\n\nThe believers used to wish for a surah about jihad to be revealed. Yet when a definitive surah was revealed mentioning fighting, the hypocrites with sickness in their hearts look at you with faint glances out of fear of death. Yet death is more fitting for them than living. Their duty was obedience and speaking righteous words. Once the matter was determined, showing loyalty would have been better for them.\n\nTo those who turned back to disbelief after the right path had become clear to them, Satan made their evils seem appealing and lured them with false hopes. That is because they said to those who disliked what Allah revealed, \"We will obey you in some matters.\" Allah knows what they conceal. How terrible will their state be when the angels take their souls, striking their faces and their backs! This is because they pursued what displeased Allah and disliked His good pleasure; thus Allah rendered their deeds worthless.\n\nAllah will surely test you until He makes evident those among you who strive in jihad and those who are patient. Those who disbelieve, bar others from the path of Allah, and oppose the Prophet can cause no harm to Allah; Allah will render their deeds worthless. O you who believe! Obey Allah and obey the Prophet, and do not render your deeds vain. Those who disbelieve and die as disbelievers, Allah will never forgive them.\n\nDo not falter and call for peace when you have the upper hand; Allah is with you, and He will not deprive you of the reward of your deeds. The worldly life is only play and amusement. If you believe and are conscious of Allah, He will grant you your rewards and will not ask you for all your wealth. Had He demanded it, you would have shown stinginess, and your rancor would have been exposed. You are being called to spend in the way of Allah; whoever is stingy harms only himself. Allah is rich (free of all needs), and you are poor. If you turn away, Allah will replace you with another people, and they will not be like you."